# Code owners: who is asked to review a pull request that touches a path.
#
# The whole tree belongs to the maintainer. GitHub requests his review on
# every pull request someone else opens; it does not make that review
# mandatory.
#
# "Require review from Code Owners" is deliberately NOT enabled in the branch
# rules for main or development. This is a one-person project and GitHub does
# not let the author of a pull request approve it, so with that rule on, no
# pull request the owner opens could ever merge. The required `ci` check is
# the gate instead (CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/RELEASING.md).
#
# The last matching pattern wins. Add narrower lines below this one only when
# a second maintainer joins.

